Work around a GCC 8 miscompilation of the NEON scale_row_grid kernel.

Verified by bisection in the LoveRetro toolchain images, holding -mcpu constant
at cortex-a53 so the compiler is the only variable:

  GCC 8.3.0  -mcpu=cortex-a53   gpu FAIL, kernels FAIL
  GCC 10.3.0 -mcpu=cortex-a53   gpu pass, kernels pass
  GCC 10.3.0 -mcpu=cortex-a55   gpu pass, kernels pass

Not an optimiser level: it reproduces at -O3, -O2 and -O1, with and without
-flto, and with -fno-strict-aliasing. tests/kernels_test.cpp reports
scale_row_grid diverging from kern::ref, and tests/gpu_test.cpp then fails every
grid, cells and chunky case with all-zero output.

Only GCC 8 falls back to the portable reference; GCC 9 and later keep the NEON
path. tg5040 and h700 build with GCC 8.3.0, tg5050 with GCC 10.3.0, so this
affects two of the three platforms and only the LCD-grid and chunky filters,
which are off in the shipped default configuration.

diff --git a/src/core/gpu/kernels_neon.cpp b/src/core/gpu/kernels_neon.cpp
index 7469114..ebb2fd5 100644
--- a/src/core/gpu/kernels_neon.cpp
+++ b/src/core/gpu/kernels_neon.cpp
@@ -905,6 +905,16 @@ void lerp_rows(const u32* a, const u32* b, u32 w, u32 n, u32* out) {
 // store's last lane costs a second bus write. Runs of two and three (every
 // scale the handhelds use) are one or two stores each.
 void scale_row_grid(const u32* src, const u16* xrun, u32 f, u32 min_run, u32 pitch, bool seam_row, u32* dst) {
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__) && __GNUC__ < 9
+  // GCC 8 miscompiles this kernel: tests/kernels_test.cpp's differential check
+  // against kern::ref finds it diverging from the portable reference, and
+  // tests/gpu_test.cpp then fails every grid, cells and chunky case. GCC 9 and
+  // later are correct, so the NEON path is kept for them and only GCC 8 falls
+  // back. The grid filter is off by default, so this costs nothing until a user
+  // turns it on, and then it is correct rather than fast.
+  ref::scale_row_grid(src, xrun, f, min_run, pitch, seam_row, dst);
+  return;
+#else
   if (min_run < 2) min_run = 2;
   if (pitch < 1) pitch = 1;
   alignas(16) u32 dimmed[256];
@@ -952,6 +962,7 @@ void scale_row_grid(const u32* src, const u16* xrun, u32 f, u32 min_run, u32 pit
     }
     }
   }
+#endif
 }
 
 
